1
00:00:00,983 --> 00:00:03,028
Capture

2
00:00:03,128 --> 00:00:08,055
Wow! I never thought we'd be meeting again like this, Peruru!

3
00:00:08,055 --> 00:00:10,944
Me neither! As soon as I heard the news, I flew right over.

4
00:00:10,944 --> 00:00:13,351
Yeah, I am pretty fast after all.

5
00:00:13,351 --> 00:00:16,564
And Crest also asked me to bring Deep Bite over ASAP.

6
00:00:16,564 --> 00:00:17,548
Thank you, Peruru.

7
00:00:17,548 --> 00:00:19,771
Where's Anna, by the way? Did she go home?

8
00:00:19,771 --> 00:00:22,239
Ah, she went to comfort the mayor.

9
00:00:22,239 --> 00:00:23,001
My approval rating...!

10
00:00:23,001 --> 00:00:26,515
- My approval rating...!
- I-it's okay! It'll go back up again in no time!

11
00:00:26,515 --> 00:00:28,992
Given how chaotic things were at the landfill, I guess it's only natural.

12
00:00:28,992 --> 00:00:31,248
Looks like being daughter of the mayor bears its own heavy burden.

13
00:00:31,248 --> 00:00:33,598
Anyway, what did you want to talk about with Deep Bite?

14
00:00:33,598 --> 00:00:37,046
Well, I summoned Deep Bite because of the cavity he once had.

15
00:00:37,046 --> 00:00:38,286
His cavity?!

16
00:00:38,286 --> 00:00:41,649
I remember Uncle Edo replaced it with a new tooth!

17
00:00:41,649 --> 00:00:43,887
What, are your teeth acting up again? Want me to take a look?

18
00:00:43,887 --> 00:00:45,625
Nah, it's not that, Edo.

19
00:00:45,625 --> 00:00:50,787
When I heard the news about the Wild Cardbots and the virus, Deep Bite's cavity immediately came to mind. Sebastian?

20
00:00:50,787 --> 00:00:51,737
Sir!

21
00:00:51,737 --> 00:00:54,500
Deep Bite went berserk because of this cavity.

22
00:00:54,500 --> 00:00:55,145
Is that... 

23
00:00:55,145 --> 00:00:58,759
And Gigantrex, who was bitten by Deep Bite, also began to malfunction. Do you remember?

24
00:00:58,759 --> 00:01:01,810
Yeah. It was a real mess. What about it?

25
00:01:01,810 --> 00:01:07,861
I compared Gigantrex's thought processor circuit data with Deep Bite's decayed tooth, and found the real cause. It was the Beast Virus! 

26
00:01:07,861 --> 00:01:08,560
What??

27
00:01:08,560 --> 00:01:09,748
What do you mean by that?

28
00:01:09,748 --> 00:01:11,646
Does that mean you were a Wild Cardbot all along?

29
00:01:11,646 --> 00:01:13,972
So that's why he looks kind of scary!

30
00:01:13,972 --> 00:01:15,829
Guys! No prejudice, please!

31
00:01:15,829 --> 00:01:19,367
Deep Bite has long suffered a lot of emotional pain because of his appearance!

32
00:01:19,367 --> 00:01:22,293
Hahahaha! It's okay. I got over it!

33
00:01:22,293 --> 00:01:23,890
Proud of ya!

34
00:01:23,890 --> 00:01:27,727
But you seem much different than a typical Wild Cardbot. Your Weapon Card is normal, for example...

35
00:01:27,727 --> 00:01:31,406
Viruses, as we understand them, cannot reproduce on their own.

36
00:01:31,406 --> 00:01:35,968
That's why they need to infiltrate a host cell and rewrite its genetic information in order to replicate themselves.

37
00:01:35,968 --> 00:01:38,528
The Beast Virus follows the same process.

38
00:01:38,528 --> 00:01:42,447
However, we've discovered that when a Metal Cardbot is infected, their genetic information is completely rewritten.

39
00:01:42,447 --> 00:01:48,864
This causes them to become aggressive and violent, and their appearance may also change depending on the virus's concentration.

40
00:01:48,864 --> 00:01:51,031
Uh... okay! I understood 100%!

41
00:01:51,031 --> 00:01:56,133
Ah, ah! Their appearance changes! L-like Blue Cop! Who also went through some changes!

42
00:01:56,133 --> 00:01:57,677
Are you sure you understood all that?

43
00:01:57,677 --> 00:02:03,387
Does that mean Deep Bite had already been infected by the Beast Virus? Even before he got a cavity?

44
00:02:03,387 --> 00:02:05,207
That may very well be the case.

45
00:02:05,207 --> 00:02:08,627
Although, I don't know how he managed to come to his senses after being infected.

46
00:02:08,627 --> 00:02:12,436
Unfortunately... I don't have any memory of when I was first infected.

47
00:02:12,436 --> 00:02:17,862
At the very least, his cavity may have been caused by a small amount of the Beast Virus that manifested very late.

48
00:02:17,862 --> 00:02:19,825
So, what are you trying to say?

49
00:02:19,825 --> 00:02:23,507
Are you saying that the bots running rampant through this city aren't pure Wild Cardbots,

50
00:02:23,507 --> 00:02:26,487
but merely Metal Cardbots infected with the virus?

51
00:02:26,487 --> 00:02:33,930
No. He means it's not one of those terrifying viruses where you're guaranteed to die once you get infected. And I'm living proof of that!

52
00:02:33,930 --> 00:02:37,229
And... getting vaccinated can prevent infection.

53
00:02:37,229 --> 00:02:38,051
What?!

54
00:02:38,051 --> 00:02:41,591
Mega Ambler! Let's work together to develop a vaccine for the Beast Virus!

55
00:02:42,191 --> 00:02:43,591
Sigh...

56
00:02:43,591 --> 00:02:45,968
As a doctor, that's an offer I can't refuse.

57
00:02:47,724 --> 00:02:49,324
I'll leave the rest up to you.

58
00:02:49,324 --> 00:02:51,263
Okay! Do your best, guys!

59
00:02:52,362 --> 00:02:56,647
Now then, the next thing we have to do is find the tank kitty and the pony with a spear.

60
00:02:56,647 --> 00:02:59,852
And we also have to find the kid who has a Metal Breath.

61
00:02:59,852 --> 00:03:01,039
Soleil, was it?

62
00:03:01,039 --> 00:03:04,627
She has two companions with her called Blaion and Phantom Hornet.

63
00:03:04,627 --> 00:03:06,280
They were both tough opponents.

64
00:03:06,280 --> 00:03:10,509
Not to mention, they also have the Beast Virus! What if they bite us and we get infected?

65
00:03:10,509 --> 00:03:12,659
I told you to stop watching zombie movies.

66
00:03:12,889 --> 00:03:15,646
Anyway, you guys be careful out there until the vaccine is developed.

67
00:03:15,646 --> 00:03:17,889
Okay. I'll go back to the fire station for now!

68
00:03:19,014 --> 00:03:20,754
Right. I need to get back to the police station as well.

69
00:03:20,754 --> 00:03:21,870
Blue Cop! Take Back!

70
00:03:21,870 --> 00:03:22,829
Huh? Wait!

71
00:03:23,957 --> 00:03:26,586
Jun, I have to get back to work too.

72
00:03:26,586 --> 00:03:29,527
Your wound isn't healed yet. Take a break for now.

73
00:03:29,527 --> 00:03:30,752
Ah... Alright.

74
00:03:30,752 --> 00:03:33,143
Blue Cop is always working himself too hard.

75
00:03:33,143 --> 00:03:34,533
It's important to take breaks, too.

76
00:03:34,533 --> 00:03:36,010
Looks like I'll have to request time off, then.

77
00:03:36,510 --> 00:03:41,344
Ugh. Man, I'm starving. I had too much fun firing my cannon nonstop.

78
00:03:41,344 --> 00:03:43,439
I wonder if there's any good places to eat around here... 

79
00:03:43,439 --> 00:03:45,634
Hm? Sniff sniff... this smell!

80
00:03:45,634 --> 00:03:47,826
That... That's gotta be delicious!

81
00:03:47,826 --> 00:03:50,396
Gotta keep my hunger on a leash until I get there!

82
00:03:53,519 --> 00:03:54,504
Welcome!

83
00:03:54,504 --> 00:03:54,889
Hey.

84
00:03:54,889 --> 00:03:56,182
Hello, officer!

85
00:03:56,182 --> 00:03:58,122
Hi. The usual, please.

86
00:03:58,122 --> 00:03:59,710
Yes sir! Coming right up.

87
00:03:59,710 --> 00:04:01,277
Jun, Why haven't I seen your friend around lately?

88
00:04:01,277 --> 00:04:02,377
Ah, well...

89
00:04:02,377 --> 00:04:03,915
Did something happen, Inspector?

90
00:04:03,915 --> 00:04:08,335
A coworker told me they've been bored lately because they haven't seen you around. Did something happen?

91
00:04:08,335 --> 00:04:10,699
It's nothing serious, sir. I'm just getting some maintenance done.

92
00:04:10,699 --> 00:04:12,086
If you say so.

93
00:04:12,086 --> 00:04:14,644
Here you go. One coffee and three 'Luecop's Donuts!

94
00:04:14,644 --> 00:04:17,463
Thank you. Ah. Actually I heard the story about the Wild Cardbots.

95
00:04:17,463 --> 00:04:18,393
How??

96
00:04:18,393 --> 00:04:22,211
Don't worry. We Mowtown police are on the Metal Cardbot's side!

97
00:04:22,211 --> 00:04:23,315
Wait a second...

98
00:04:23,315 --> 00:04:25,319
Was it you, Anna?!

99
00:04:25,319 --> 00:04:29,394
I couldn't help it! It was so hard trying to comfort my dad!

100
00:04:29,394 --> 00:04:32,170
He sees right through everything, so lying won't work on him, so I...!

101
00:04:32,170 --> 00:04:36,158
Don't be too hard on her, Jun. You know there's a heavy burden on Anna's shoulders. Isn't that right?

102
00:04:36,158 --> 00:04:39,269
That's right! Bleeehh~!

103
00:04:39,269 --> 00:04:43,959
Ahahaha... it'll be alright. There's no point in hiding the truth now.

104
00:04:43,959 --> 00:04:46,211
All right, then. I'm going to head back now.

105
00:04:46,211 --> 00:04:46,954
Already?

106
00:04:46,954 --> 00:04:50,088
I just popped in for a quick visit. I also have a lot of things to do, you know.

107
00:04:50,088 --> 00:04:52,459
Gotta take care of the big guys from the Sea of Stars.

108
00:04:52,459 --> 00:04:54,629
By the way, Jun, thanks for the spear.

109
00:04:54,629 --> 00:04:57,192
Hehehe... I kept it nice and safe at my house just for you.

110
00:04:57,192 --> 00:05:01,559
Well then, take good care of Deep Bite. And make sure you do a good job helping with the vaccine research.

111
00:05:01,559 --> 00:05:03,487
Alright, alright.

112
00:05:03,487 --> 00:05:05,689
Cielo, send my regards to everyone.

113
00:05:05,689 --> 00:05:06,987
Will do. Don't worry about it.

114
00:05:06,987 --> 00:05:09,317
Ugh, such a shame to see you go so soon. Share those with everyone, okay?

115
00:05:09,317 --> 00:05:10,627
B-be careful on the way out!

116
00:05:10,627 --> 00:05:13,615
Haha... Thank you for the food! Cielo, I need you to be my eyes!

117
00:05:13,615 --> 00:05:15,916
Okay. Keep going straight!

118
00:05:15,916 --> 00:05:19,125
Yawn... Welcome...

119
00:05:19,125 --> 00:05:21,665
One Dexdex Honey Dip and one Buffy Cream donut, please.

120
00:05:21,665 --> 00:05:23,290
Uh... is that Soleil?

121
00:05:24,490 --> 00:05:25,733
Why are you here?!

122
00:05:25,733 --> 00:05:27,120
For here or to go?

123
00:05:27,120 --> 00:05:28,110
To go, please.

124
00:05:28,110 --> 00:05:32,021
Sure thing, right away. When did you make friends with such a cute girl?

125
00:05:32,021 --> 00:05:33,805
M-Mom!

126
00:05:33,805 --> 00:05:35,848
Do you have any idea how long we've been looking for you?!

127
00:05:35,848 --> 00:05:37,757
I know. That's why I have been hiding.

128
00:05:37,757 --> 00:05:43,038
Grrr... A friend told me that a person doesn't run and hide unless they know they did something wrong!

129
00:05:43,038 --> 00:05:44,271
Here you go.

130
00:05:44,271 --> 00:05:45,488
Thank you.

131
00:05:46,254 --> 00:05:47,153
Wait!

132
00:05:47,153 --> 00:05:48,819
We won't let you go so easily!

133
00:05:48,819 --> 00:05:49,413
Right!

134
00:05:49,413 --> 00:05:53,185
We only came here for donuts... What should we do, Blaion?

135
00:05:53,185 --> 00:05:54,154
Look.

136
00:05:54,254 --> 00:05:56,396
(Breaking news! A major fire has broken out at the Cassias Oil Refinery, located in the northwestern part of Mowtown!)

137
00:05:56,495 --> 00:06:03,814
The oil refinery is engulfed in thick black smoke and flames. Firefighters are working hard to put out the fire, but the flames are proving difficult to control.

138
00:06:03,814 --> 00:06:08,031
Uh-Wait a minute. Uh... that's a Metal Cardbot! We have a visual of a Metal Cardbot with two axes!

139
00:06:08,132 --> 00:06:08,812
That's...!

140
00:06:08,812 --> 00:06:09,906
...Tigun!

141
00:06:09,906 --> 00:06:12,169
(Fire authorities dispatched Phoenix Fire, a Metal Cardbot firefighter, on an emergency call, and...)

142
00:06:12,169 --> 00:06:13,711
- (Fire authorities dispatched Phoenix Fire, a Metal Cardbot firefighter, on an emergency call, and...)
- Ah!

143
00:06:13,711 --> 00:06:14,843
Soleil!

144
00:06:14,843 --> 00:06:15,987
Jun! Let's go!

145
00:06:15,987 --> 00:06:16,807
Yeah!

146
00:06:17,963 --> 00:06:18,701
We should go too!

147
00:06:18,701 --> 00:06:21,923
Theo and Anna, you two stay here and eat more donuts!

148
00:06:21,923 --> 00:06:24,047
Take care of my son out there, Bluey.

149
00:06:24,047 --> 00:06:25,391
Leave it to me, ma'am.

150
00:06:32,158 --> 00:06:32,870
Is everyone okay?

151
00:06:32,870 --> 00:06:33,963
All thanks to you!

152
00:06:33,963 --> 00:06:37,627
Alright! We got ahead of Blaion! We're here first!

153
00:06:37,627 --> 00:06:39,475
This isn't a race, Jun.

154
00:06:39,475 --> 00:06:41,521
Oh, it's Phoenix Fire!

155
00:06:41,521 --> 00:06:42,576
How's it going?

156
00:06:42,576 --> 00:06:47,062
Jun! Blue Cop! The tank bot stole some oil from here and now he's causing a ruckus!

157
00:06:47,062 --> 00:06:48,797
Looks like he's no ordinary glutton.

158
00:06:48,797 --> 00:06:50,024
Jun, what should we do?

159
00:06:50,024 --> 00:06:54,622
We're going in. We have a pro firefighter with us. There's nothing to be afraid of.

160
00:06:54,622 --> 00:06:58,071
Except I'm really afraid! If you underestimate fire, you'll be in for a rude awakening!

161
00:06:58,071 --> 00:06:59,792
Sorry. I'll get serious.

162
00:06:59,792 --> 00:07:02,529
Why don't you let me sweep everything away with my water vortex?

163
00:07:02,529 --> 00:07:05,836
We should save that for later, we can't use that move too often. Let's stick to the plan.

164
00:07:05,836 --> 00:07:06,793
Alrighty!

165
00:07:06,793 --> 00:07:07,829
Where's Tigun?

166
00:07:07,829 --> 00:07:09,088
He's inside, but...

167
00:07:09,088 --> 00:07:11,185
Leave this to us. You go on ahead!

168
00:07:11,185 --> 00:07:12,966
Yes, sir! Follow me!

169
00:07:13,447 --> 00:07:15,059
Heh heh...

170
00:07:16,156 --> 00:07:20,711
The oil here tastes light and mild and real good. Hahaha!

171
00:07:20,711 --> 00:07:24,365
So let's drink some more! Hahahaha!

172
00:07:24,365 --> 00:07:25,505
Stop right there!

173
00:07:25,505 --> 00:07:28,648
Going on a rampage in a dangerous place like this... don't you value your life at all?!

174
00:07:28,648 --> 00:07:33,848
Grr... What? Oil doesn't taste as good without a little thrill!

175
00:07:33,848 --> 00:07:38,012
When we're hungry, we eat! And then we get wild and more wild!

176
00:07:38,012 --> 00:07:40,978
That's the very instinct of my kind... the Wild Cardbots!

177
00:07:40,978 --> 00:07:42,302
If he fires that cannon in a place like this...!

178
00:07:42,302 --> 00:07:42,845
Blue Cop!

179
00:07:42,845 --> 00:07:43,667
On it!

180
00:07:48,947 --> 00:07:52,483
Since we have to live alongside the people who have taken us in...

181
00:07:52,483 --> 00:07:54,817
we can't let you run wild as you please, Tigun!

182
00:07:54,817 --> 00:07:58,504
If that's your instinct, then you follow that!

183
00:08:02,187 --> 00:08:03,560
One more!

184
00:08:03,560 --> 00:08:05,204
Deep Bite! Bite deep!

185
00:08:09,333 --> 00:08:11,163
Phoenix Fire! Set Up!

186
00:08:12,790 --> 00:08:14,762
Burning Hammer!

187
00:08:16,427 --> 00:08:17,976
Heh! You can't hurt me with that toy hammer-

188
00:08:17,976 --> 00:08:19,225
BRUGUBRRRRRRR!

189
00:08:19,225 --> 00:08:20,817
Stay still!

190
00:08:20,817 --> 00:08:23,298
Your turn now! Deep Bite! Set Up!

191
00:08:25,005 --> 00:08:27,976
Let me cool that head of yours, kitty cat!

192
00:08:36,337 --> 00:08:37,644
We have backup?

193
00:08:38,790 --> 00:08:41,227
I think that'll do it if he's that waterlogged, Jun.

194
00:08:41,227 --> 00:08:43,280
Right! Blue Cop, let's finish this!

195
00:08:43,280 --> 00:08:43,880
Yes!

196
00:08:48,182 --> 00:08:51,826
You little...! I'm not here for a squirt gun fight!

197
00:08:52,826 --> 00:08:53,730
What the...?

198
00:08:53,730 --> 00:08:57,027
Heh heh... Blue Cop is skilled in handling electricity.

199
00:08:57,027 --> 00:09:01,923
You know what happens if you get hit by his attack when you're soaking wet, right?

200
00:09:01,923 --> 00:09:02,750
I dunno.

201
00:09:02,750 --> 00:09:03,681
Seriously?

202
00:09:03,681 --> 00:09:05,690
Alpha Bolt...

203
00:09:05,690 --> 00:09:07,101
...Cannon!

204
00:09:17,416 --> 00:09:20,163
Hahahaha! How'd ya like our teamwork?

205
00:09:20,163 --> 00:09:21,443
Alright!

206
00:09:21,443 --> 00:09:22,518
Huh?

207
00:09:24,437 --> 00:09:26,044
Phantom Hornet!

208
00:09:26,044 --> 00:09:27,370
Wild Cardbot!

209
00:09:28,322 --> 00:09:29,697
Change...

210
00:09:33,460 --> 00:09:35,975
Huh? Soleil!

211
00:09:35,975 --> 00:09:37,556
Don't you go stealing our prey!

212
00:09:40,036 --> 00:09:42,063
Phantom Hornet. Set Up.

213
00:09:42,995 --> 00:09:43,884
Bzzzt!

214
00:09:44,239 --> 00:09:45,749
Deep Bite! Set Up!

215
00:09:48,951 --> 00:09:50,009
Veno Spear.

216
00:09:52,576 --> 00:09:53,740
Deep Bite!

217
00:09:58,418 --> 00:10:01,005
Soleil! Why are you doing this?!

218
00:10:01,005 --> 00:10:03,005
It's my mother's wish.

219
00:10:04,605 --> 00:10:06,261
Blaion. Set Up.

220
00:10:21,081 --> 00:10:22,979
Fire Roar Blaze.

221
00:10:22,979 --> 00:10:25,003
Fire Roar...

222
00:10:27,267 --> 00:10:28,457
Blaze!

223
00:10:37,254 --> 00:10:38,390
Change Up.

224
00:10:47,575 --> 00:10:49,899
Deep Bite. Sealed.

225
00:10:49,899 --> 00:10:52,658
I'm going to take your friend with me today.

226
00:10:53,359 --> 00:10:55,830
Bzzt. I don't see Tigun.

227
00:10:55,830 --> 00:10:59,759
Darn. Did he get away? I can't believe he still had the strength to move after that. He's resilient.

228
00:10:59,759 --> 00:11:03,287
He must be overflowing with energy since he drank his fill of oil.

229
00:11:05,832 --> 00:11:08,139
Give us back our comrade Deep Bite!

230
00:11:08,139 --> 00:11:10,628
I'm just following the will of my benefactors!

231
00:11:10,628 --> 00:11:12,304
Let's go now, Blaion.

232
00:11:12,304 --> 00:11:13,402
Got it.

233
00:11:15,668 --> 00:11:18,181
Omega Heat Flame!

234
00:11:27,332 --> 00:11:29,527
Jun! Are you alright?!

235
00:11:29,527 --> 00:11:31,158
Deep Bite...!

